          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 23:29:54.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20287 tests: handle IDIF FIDs in ost_fid2_objpath()",
        "message": "LU-20287 tests: handle IDIF FIDs in ost_fid2_objpath()\n\nsanity test_39v failed in every interop session with 2.15 servers\nwith \"OST0 uid:gid : != 500:500\".  A 2.15 OST gives MDT0 objects\nIDIF FIDs like [0x100000000:0x42e:0x0], which ost_fid2_objpath()\nturned into O/100000000/d14/42e, so debugfs could not find the\nobject to check its owner.\n\nAn IDIF FID holds the OST index and the high 16 bits of a 48-bit\nobject id in its sequence, and the object is stored in O/0 under\nits decimal object id.  Return that path for an IDIF FID, so 39v\nand the other callers of ost_fid2_objpath() work with such OSTs.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity serverversion=2.15 env=ONLY=39v\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Id9e222f5ad61e75162ecfe2f5d8981dc543ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
